# Line-ending policy.
#
# The default (no `text` attribute, no `core.autocrlf`) stores bytes as committed,
# which is what the corpus below depends on. This file exists to make that a
# *decision* rather than a property of whoever happened to commit first — a
# contributor on Windows, or anyone adding `* text=auto`, would otherwise normalise
# these two files and silently delete the thing they are for.

# CRLF ON PURPOSE. Every other document in data/demo/ is LF, so nothing in the corpus
# could exercise a \r-sensitive code path. That is not hypothetical: the locate() fix
# in #90 hinged on \r, and the version proposed in #86 omitted it — which would have
# silently failed to locate every quote in a CRLF document, dropping edges rather than
# erroring. 461 tests passed and the mechanism gate was byte-identical.
#
# `tests/test_corpus_properties.py` asserts these are still CRLF. If that test fails,
# something normalised them; restore the line endings rather than relaxing the test.
data/demo/messy_board_meeting_17_transcript.txt -text
data/demo/messy_vendor_followup_email.md        -text
